    "sourceUrl": "https://www.techpowerup.com/354543/amd-goes-data-center-first-while-gaming-revenue-drops-40",
    "publishedAt": "2026-11-06",
    "summary": "Here's how she put it: Dr. Lisa Su, AMD CEO We are a data center first company, that is our profile, and you know, people need more computing to power all these applications. Data Center brought in a record $8.5 billion in Q3, up 97%, and now makes up 64% of AMD's $13.4 billion total, up from 47% a year ago. Gaming fell to $773 million, or under 6% of revenue. Gaming was flat against Q2, though, and last year's Q3 was boosted by a 181% console-driven jump to $1.3 billion.",
    "whyItMatters": "10-K/10-Q 要重点抽取资本开支、库存、客户集中度、毛利和风险因素，不能只停留在 filing 本身。",
